# Sites that invoke external IO directly inside a with_lock critical section.
# Format: <path>:<line>:<kind>|why=<one-line justification>
# Shrink-only: new sites fail CI, and an entry that no longer matches a site fails
# too, so the inventory can only get smaller. Remove an entry when the read moves
# outside the lock and only the currency re-check plus its protected write remain.
#
# "justified" means the in-lock IO IS the protected write this lock exists to
# serialize, not a read-for-decision. "needs-redesign" means the safe shrink is more
# than a mechanical application of the principle and is tracked separately.
packages/github-devloop-integration/departments/sync_scan/main.lua:196:forge_handle|why=justified: the critical section IS the branch-pair merge-and-push it serializes; key is github-devloop/branch-sync/<repo>/<upstream>/<integration>, disjoint from the per-entity transition keys
packages/github-devloop-integration/departments/pr_freshness_scan/main.lua:332:forge_handle|why=justified: the critical section IS the managed-branch refresh push it serializes; key is github-devloop/pr-freshness/<repo>/<branch>, disjoint from the per-entity transition keys
packages/github-devloop-integration/departments/sync_conflict/main.lua:544:forge_handle|why=needs-redesign(#3520-class): conflict resolution reads and pushes under one branch-pair lock; splitting it needs a per-effect currency design, not a mechanical move
packages/github-devloop-integration/departments/sync_conflict/main.lua:544:spawn_codex|why=needs-redesign(#3520-class): the resolver codex runs inside the branch-pair lock; moving it out requires re-validating the conflict base at commit rather than relying on the hold
